requirements.detail:
Categorizes flood damages into five distinct, standard auditing classes:
a) Agricultural crops;
b) Private and public properties;
c) Business and other secondary activities;
d) Spread of epidemics, ill health, and loss of livestock; and
e) Fear, anxiety, and distress.

Mandates organizing actual field investigation work into four distinct operational phases:
1) Primary investigation into the nature of plots (initiated prior to floods);
2) Pre-flood enquiry;
3) Field work during floods; and
4) Assessment of damages.

Specifies mapping and classifying land plots into six core types prior to flooding:
a) Cultivable;
b) Cultivable waste;
c) Orchards;
d) Residential;\ e) Ponds or tanks; and
f) Bushes and pastures.
